                <pb facs="0258" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.4227/54</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Canadian Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Massey</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-10-22">October 22, 1929</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 207</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to refer to your note of
                    August 29th, 1929, concerning the proposed reciprocal arrangement between the
                    United States and Canada for the admission of civil aircraft, the issuance of
                    pilots’ licenses, and the acceptance of certificates of airworthiness for
                    aircraft imported as merchandise. I have been instructed to inform you that His
                    Majesty’s Government in Canada concur in the terms of the agreement as set forth
                    in your note, and will, therefore, consider it to be operative from this
                    date.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Vincent Massey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
